  {
    "episode_id": 64508,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/4/64508.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, the genesis of the book, and I really didn't know when I began thinking of this, that it would go the ultimate direction that it did. The genesis of the book was, of course, a very painful time in my life when I lost a four-year-old grandson in a tragic fire. I mean, I remember it like it was yesterday. God has put a lot of love and anointing oil on those wounds because they were deep. They were hurtful. I remember the feelings of helplessness and just questioning everything. How could something like this happen? And there was no one to blame. There wasn't a person that I could point a finger at and say, why did you do this to my grandson? It was an accident and it happened. And so I felt like I was a drift for so long until, and I'd been a Christian my entire life since I was about 10 years old. And so I knew that bad things happened to good people. But even though I was strong in my faith, I had never had to process it. that way. But God showed up for me. He showed up for me over time, and He spoke to my heart as only the Spirit can, that I'm not going to get answers here about why that happened to my grandson and my son-in-law. I will find out when I see Christ. I'll be able to ask him, and he'll be able to tell me. But I don't need to worry about that here. What I determined to do in the book was to let my experiences of regeneration rebuilding, getting regrounded in your faith to let that be a light to someone who might be struggling. That's what the book was about. I know there's some funny parts in it. There's some goofy parts in it because I lived a very goofy childhood. That's what it's all about. It's really all about reconnecting with the person's faith. And it's designed to focus on men and help them understand the critical role that they play in the life of a child. I tell people this all the time. The first institution that God created was the family. He said, for this reason, men and women will leave their parents and come together and build a family, and they shall become one. And that's where it all begins. And God had a purpose in why He put the two pieces of the puzzle together the way that He did, the role of the Father. is very different than the role of the mother, but equally important in the life of a child. And in today's culture, oh my goodness, we have millions and millions of children that are growing up in single parents, single mother homes, or being raised by grandparents with no father figure around. And they are missing that critical linkage because we learn how our Heavenly Father loves us through the actions of our earthly fathers.",
