    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, there are many more that stood in the gap for me at various times and places in my life than what I could put in the book. I chose some of the few, you know, my earliest memories as a child. And my mother actually, when she first read the manuscript, she got a little bit offended, actually, because I gave my grandparents, particularly my grandfather, a lot of credit for my early foundations in my faith. And that's because that was my experience. And Mom had no way of knowing how that was going to affect me. But my granddad was a superintendent of a little church, a little country church, one room, maybe I think two classrooms in the back. But he would take me with him. He was the superintendent of the Sunday School, and he would take me with him. to signal the start of Sunday school, which was to ring the bell in the steeple of that little country church. And so he would let me, he would pull it down and let me hold on to the rope and the bell was big. So it would just pull me off the ground and it would sling me into the rafters. And it was like, for me, I was like going to Disney World",
